        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-06 00:43:51.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-9 lod: allocate MDT stripes by weighted round-robin",
        "message": "LU-9 lod: allocate MDT stripes by weighted round-robin\n\nThe stripes of a new striped directory are allocated on MDTs chosen\nat random, weighted by their free space and inodes less a penalty\nfor recently used MDTs and MDSs.  Like the random OST allocation\nbefore, this spreads the stripes unevenly over short runs, and the\npenalties need tuning to work against the randomness.\n\nAllocate the remote MDT stripes in lod_mdt_alloc_qos() by weighted\nround-robin over the round-robin array, like OST objects.  The same\nltd_qos_wrr_weights() adjusts the weights by mdt_qos_prio_free and\ncaps them so that no MDT gets more than one stripe of a directory.\nThe MDT penalties are no longer used.  Leave the existing stripes of a\ndirectory being split out of the weights, and skip inactive MDTs,\nwhich are not in the round-robin array.\n\nAdd lod.*.mdt_qos_wrr_enable to fall back to picking the MDTs at\nrandom by weight, as for OSTs.\n\nUpdate the man pages for the MDT parameters.  Add sanity test_413m to\ncheck the balance of the remote stripes over the MDTs.\n\nCreating 300 2-stripe directories on 4 MDTs, with stripe 0 placed\nround-robin by the client and mdt_qos_threshold_rr=0, gives these\nsecond stripes per MDT in total (wanted 75, or about 67 on MDT3 with\n15% fewer free inodes) and per 30 directories (wanted 7-8):\n\n                            before            after\n                            total  per 30     total  per 30\n  equal MDTs                69-81  3-12       74-76  6-9\n  MDT3 15% fewer inodes     65-84  3-13       67-79  5-10\n\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5.5 ltvm,llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Ia09f0945a30f6fd6ef95dd8902725e5a493ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
